# Results vs Discussion

Results (publication §6) report what was tested and what the numbers are.
Discussion (§7) interprets. Do not put design implications, H1–H3 claims,
“what this means for ads/trust,” “precise null vs dead pipeline,” or
“do not put this in the abstract” into Results.

EEG Results (`sec:results-eeg`) is confirmatory numbers, tables, forests.
EEG interpretation lives in Discussion `sec:disc-eeg` (paper and thesis).
A literature-ROI / channel-set rebuild is sensitivity only; do not put
it in confirmatory Results or the abstract. Appendix
`sec:app-eeg-channel-sets` (paper and thesis) is the allowed mention.
Trajectory theory, Results, and Discussion are **thesis-only**
(`chp:theory`, `sec:results-trajectories`, `sec:disc-trajectories`).
Do not put them back in the paper.

